Z||000000||Bill Shenefelt||12-31-2001||10:33 AM||||Not wanting to do any real mods to the car, I installed a system in my 86 that beats anything I ever heard.  I just finished moving it to another 86 due to problems with my original car.  The amps are kicker 120's Speakers Diamond Acoustics 6.5's with aluminum dome tweeters and the head unit is a Sony tape with minidisk changer.  The subwoofer is crossed with an alpine equalizer/ sub crossover.<BR>Speakers really need boxes to sound their best.  This is not a "boom box" unit to disturb homes and shake windows you drive by, but is a real nice hi fi sound. ps, you do need to have short legs though.  At least under 6 ft or it could be cramped. The units behind the seats are just short of the upright glove box console.  I could not get the boxes any thinner and still have the magnets fit the boxes.<BR>I have not heard better speakers than the Diamonds, with or without a subwoofer.  They go down to a true 60 cps solid and crisp if you use good boxes made of 3/4 inch high density particle board. As for the no cut part, I did have to remove the little upright behind the stock radio as you must do with most aftermarket radios, but that is it.  A photo form the passenger door is posted at <A HREF="http://shene.killi.net/fierosystem.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://shene.killi.net/fierosystem.jpg</A> <BR>and one from the driver door at <A HREF="http://shene.killi.net/fierosystem" TARGET=_blank>http://shene.killi.net/fierosystem</A>  view2.jpg<BR>I have home built JBL studio monitor horn systems in my house and these are very similar in sound quality.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Bill Shenefelt||||reg||1
